 - Multiclass top-label ECE/MCE depend on equal-width bins and can hide class-conditional miscalibration. Proper scoring rules and class-specific inspection should accompany them.
 - Sidak/Hochberg require independence or suitable positive dependence for their advertised family-wise guarantees. Benjamini-Yekutieli is valid under arbitrary dependence but conservative. Storey q-values condition on a caller-declared lambda and its estimated null fraction.
 - Pairwise distance and kernel matrices are bounded at 25,000,000 elements; larger requests fail with `ComputationTooLarge`.
+
+## v1.2 distributional and network scope
+
+- Linear quantile regression minimizes the Koenker-Bassett check loss through a
+  deterministic ADMM solver. It reports optimization residuals but does not
+  fabricate coefficient standard errors; bootstrap or asymptotic uncertainty
+  must be selected explicitly by the caller.
+- Expectile regression uses asymmetric least-squares IRLS. Expectiles are
+  tail-sensitive conditional location functionals and are not probabilities or
+  quantiles.
+- Gamma regression uses a log link and the gamma variance function. Dispersion
+  is estimated from deviance over residual degrees of freedom; shape is its
+  reciprocal. Outcomes must be finite and strictly positive.
+- Gaussian location-scale regression alternates inverse-variance weighted mean
+  fitting with Fisher scoring for a log-linear variance. The reported scale
+  covariance is the expected-information approximation under the fitted
+  Gaussian model.
+- Random-intercept regression profiles the ratio of random-intercept to
+  residual variance under Gaussian compound symmetry. v1.2 supports one random
+  intercept, not random slopes, crossed effects, REML, or non-Gaussian outcomes.
+- Beta-binomial and known-variance normal Bayes factors depend on the declared
+  priors. WAIC uses the sample variance of pointwise log likelihood across
+  posterior draws and is unreliable when posterior tails or influential
+  observations invalidate its asymptotic approximation.
+- Weighted-network inputs are dense, finite, non-negative adjacency matrices.
+  Undirected graphs must be symmetric and self loops are rejected. Weights are
+  treated as strengths for PageRank and modularity, while hop, clustering, and
+  Brandes diagnostics use positive-edge topology.
+- Network label-permutation tests preserve each graph's topology and permute
+  node correspondence. Their interpretation requires exchangeable labels under
+  the null; spatial, temporal, or design constraints must be encoded outside
+  the generic QAP-style procedure.
+- Pinball, expectile, interval, and CRPS values are comparative proper or
+  task-specific scores. Their magnitude depends on the outcome scale and should
+  be reported against meaningful baselines on held-out observations.
