+# v1.2 validation record
+
+This record describes the checks performed on the `symthaea-statistics` v1.2
+release candidate in the artifact environment.
+
+## Source surface
+
+- 118 public modules plus one private model-matrix module
+- 633 resolved root exports
+- 120 Rust source files and 24 integration-test files
+- 493 `#[test]` functions present in source and integration tests
+- no `unsafe` token outside the crate-level prohibition
+- no production `unwrap`, `expect`, `panic!`, or `unreachable!` surface
+- every declared module has a matching source file and every module file is declared
+- every item in the stable v1 prelude resolves through the root export surface
+- `API_LEVEL = 1` and `NUMERICAL_CONTRACT = "validated-v1"` remain unchanged
+
+## Syntax and repository checks
+
+- all 144 Rust source and integration-test files parse without tree-sitter error nodes
+- `git diff --check` passes
+- the independent v1.2 reference generator reproduces its committed JSON byte-for-byte
+- the stable-prelude compatibility integration tests are present
+
+## Independent numerical landmarks
+
+The retained generator uses NumPy, SciPy, statsmodels, scikit-learn, and
+NetworkX to record independent values for:
+
+- median quantile-regression coefficients and check-loss objective
+- asymmetric intercept-only expectiles
+- gamma log-link coefficients, deviance, and deviance dispersion
+- joint Gaussian mean and log-variance coefficients
+- Gaussian random-intercept fixed effects, residual variance, group variance,
+  and maximum likelihood
+- exact beta-binomial Bayes factors
+- WAIC pointwise and aggregate components
+- weighted PageRank, closeness, Brandes betweenness, and planted-partition
+  modularity
+- Gaussian continuous ranked probability score
+
+The Rust integration vectors bind those values with explicit numerical
+tolerances. Seeded network permutations and optimization APIs also carry
+reproducibility and adversarial contract tests.
+
+## Resource and contract hardening
+
+The v1.2 layer rejects rank-deficient conditional models, non-positive gamma
+outcomes, invalid quantile/expectile levels, ragged pointwise likelihood draws,
+integer evidence counts above exact `f64` representation, non-finite network
+row strength, negative weights, self loops, asymmetric undirected inputs,
+invalid PageRank settings, mismatched community assignments, unreplicated
+random-intercept designs, and reversed forecast intervals.
+
+Network topology and weight semantics are explicit: weights are strengths for
+PageRank and modularity, while hop, clustering, and Brandes methods use positive
+edge presence. QAP-style tests require explicit seeds and add-one Monte Carlo
+p-values.
+
+## Unavailable checks
+
+The environment contains Rustup launchers but no installed Rust toolchain and
+cannot resolve an outbound toolchain download. Therefore Cargo compilation,
+execution of the 493 Rust tests, Clippy, rustfmt, rustdoc, and `cargo package`
+were not performed here. `scripts/verify.sh` remains the authoritative Rust
+1.85+ verification lane, and `scripts/verify_v1_2_references.sh` is the separate
+Python reference-regeneration lane.
